# Google Identity Services (GIS) credentials for Drive integration.
#
# BusinessVault uses the browser-only GIS token flow — NO client secret,
# NO redirect URI, NO server callback. The user consents in a Google popup;
# an access token is returned to the page and never leaves the browser
# (stored in a private IndexedDB).
#
# Scope used: https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file (per-file access;
# BusinessVault can only see files it creates).
#
# Setup (Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials → Create OAuth
# client ID → Web application):
#   1. Application type: Web application
#   2. Authorized JavaScript origins: add each host you serve from, e.g.
#        http://localhost:5173
#        https://bhawnajain1.github.io
#      DO NOT add any Authorized redirect URI — GIS does not use one.
#   3. Copy the "Client ID" into VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID below.
#
# Vite exposes any variable prefixed with VITE_ to the client bundle.
# NEVER commit .env or .env.local with real values.

VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-oauth-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
